{"proposal":{"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.22174c64a9d2bb1c3da83ec8.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Responsibility for soundness and record keeping carries a substantive performance component when read with the express requirement to ensure proper records and compatibility.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.22174c64a9d2bb1c3da83ec8.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The text does not establish strict liability for every incident or an absolute guarantee against failure.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":null,"controlled_language":"Read substantively with the requirement to ensure proper ownership records and operational compatibility, paragraph 10 requires retained accountability exercised so that management, operations and record keeping meet the applicable standard. A fulfillment conclusion would require evidence of retained authority, effective supervisory conduct and satisfactory operational and record-keeping performance. The excerpts do not supply a complete standard or facts permitting that conclusion.","family_ids":["modality"],"parent_id":null,"revision_reason":"Unlike the allocation-focused reading, this reading requires evidence of satisfactory substantive performance to conclude that paragraph 10 itself is fulfilled. Authority and diligent supervision are relevant but cannot substitute for the required operational and record-keeping condition.","source_packet_hash":"d74180e126dda06342060a17b37c3227fc695e9fc0f0d5ce68b187d7cb8bc612","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u1.224","dc689bdf0ffcf.u2.729","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185"],"subject_unit":"Paragraph 10 and footnote 1: substantive fulfillment"},"reason":"Reserve space for unexplored families","run_id":"run.8adc12b432874c5bb1e8b4730a0ab93f"}